// EFI-unofficial tutorial index (split format)
// Minecraft 1.20.1 | Forge 47.4.0
//
// This file is a quick map. The actual tutorials are split into:
//
// 1) Core / baseline behavior tutorial:
//    tutorial - core - 1.20.1 - en_us.json
//
// 2) Extension features tutorial:
//    tutorial - extensions - 1.20.1 - en_us.json
//
// Why split?
// - Core file explains the original/base behavior surface and base predicates.
// - Extensions file explains what EFI adds on top (NBT tag path, TACZ helpers,
//   ammo routing, gear swap, and extension predicates/behaviors).
//
// Notes:
// - TACZ is an optional extension, not the centerpiece.
// - nbt_tag is also an extension path, alternative to registry-path-keyed files.
// - Base Epic Fight datapack logic remains valid and supported.
// - Native held-item living motions are used when humanoid_weapon_motions is omitted.
//
// CNPC quick start (actual addon schema):
// 1. Put the patch at data/customnpcs/npc_epicfight_mobpatch/customnpc.json.
// 2. In the NPC script write a marker:
//      function init(e) { e.npc.setEFNbtMarker("efi_role", "ranged"); }
// 3. Match it in the patch with:
//      "nbt_tag": "{ForgeData:{efi_role:\"ranged\"}}"
// 4. Include attributes.max_stun_shield and a stun_animations object.
// 5. Use "bow"/"crossbow" for ranged weapon_categories; "ranged" is obsolete.
// 6. Test stun with an Epic Fight combat-mode attack. Vanilla damage produces
//    vanilla knockback but does not create an EpicFightDamageSource.
// 7. The same nbt_tag file can be shared by any number of mobs or CNPCs.
// 8. For TACZ, use a looping tacz_aim -> tacz_shoot series and add reload
//    branches for both has_target and no_target when idle reload is desired.
//
// Final quick test:
// - /reload after changing a patch
// - spawn two entities with the same nbt_tag marker
// - verify native held-item motions when humanoid_weapon_motions is omitted
// - verify Epic Fight hit_short/hit_long, knockdown, fall, and neutralize
// - verify aim remains active until the firing cycle reloads
